     fhir:CodeSystem.concept.definition [ fhir:value "Liquid, single-dose or multidose preparation consisting of a suspension intended for oral use, showing a slower release of the active substance(s) than that of a conventional-release oral suspension. This deliberate modification is achieved by a special formulation design and/or manufacturing method. Each dose from a multidose container is administered by means of a device suitable for measuring the prescribed volume. The device is usually a spoon or a cup for volumes of 5 mL or multiples thereof or an oral syringe for other volumes." ] ;
